   "about": "I like understanding how things work. Whether it's a distributed system, a production issue that's been around for months, or a new piece of technology, I usually end up digging into the details until it makes sense.\nI've spent the last 9 years building software with .NET and Azure, working on everything from legacy modernization to cloud applications and APIs. Lately I've been spending more time on architecture, observability, AI developer tooling, and the kinds of engineering problems that don't have an obvious answer.\nI enjoy being hands-on, but I also like helping teams make good technical decisions. That could be reviewing a design, mentoring another developer, improving deployment pipelines, or tracking down a production issue that everyone else has given up on.\nI'm always interested in learning something new and building software that's simpler, more reliable, and easier for the next developer to work on.",
